# SECURITY WARNING: OAuth Token Protection
# =========================================
# This .gitignore file is CRITICAL for preventing accidental exposure of
# Shopify access tokens and other sensitive credentials.
# 
# NEVER remove or modify these patterns without careful security review.
# Token exposure can lead to:
# - Unauthorized access to merchant stores
# - Data breaches and privacy violations
# - API abuse and rate limiting issues
# - Compliance violations (GDPR, PCI, etc.)
#
# If you accidentally commit any of these files:
# 1. Immediately rotate/revoke the exposed tokens
# 2. Remove the files from git history using git filter-branch or BFG
# 3. Force push to all remotes
# 4. Notify security team and affected merchants

# OAuth Token Files - NEVER COMMIT
# ================================
# These patterns catch common token file naming conventions
captured_token.json
*_access_token.json
*.token
access_token*
oauth_token*
api_secret*
shopify_token*
token.json
tokens.json
credentials.json
auth.json
*.key
*.pem
*.cert

# Environment Files - CONTAIN SECRETS
# ===================================
# Environment files often contain API keys, secrets, and tokens
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.test
.env.staging
env.json
config.json
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml

# Log Files - MAY CONTAIN TOKENS
# ===============================
# Logs can accidentally contain sensitive data from debugging
*.log
logs/
*.log.*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
access.log
error.log
debug.log

# Temporary and Cache Files
# =========================
# These might contain cached tokens or sensitive data
.cache/
.tmp/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# IDE and Editor Files
# ====================
# May contain sensitive project configuration
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build and Distribution
# ======================
# Compiled code might contain embedded secrets
dist/
build/
out/

# Node.js Dependencies
# ====================
# Dependencies are installed locally, not committed
node_modules/

# Test Coverage and Reports
# =========================
# May contain sensitive test data
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
junit.xml

# Session and State Files
# =======================
# May contain active session tokens
session.json
sessions/
*.session
state.json

# Database Files
# ==============
# Local databases may contain tokens
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ADDITIONAL SECURITY NOTES
# ========================
# 1. Always use environment variables for secrets in production
# 2. Implement token rotation policies
# 3. Use secure token storage (e.g., encrypted database, secret management service)
# 4. Monitor for exposed tokens in git history
# 5. Enable GitHub secret scanning
# 6. Regularly audit this .gitignore file
#
# For questions about security practices, consult:
# - Shopify App Security Best Practices
# - OWASP Security Guidelines
# - Your organization's security team